_A data structure is a way of organizing and storing data in a program so that it can be used efficiently.

_A sorting algorithm is a method used to organize data in a specific order (ascending or descending).

_Data structures I am not yet familiar with:

Linked Lists – I still don’t fully understand how nodes are connected using pointers.
Trees (especially Binary Trees) – I find it difficult to visualize how the data is structured hierarchically.
Graphs – I am not yet comfortable with concepts like nodes, edges, and traversal algorithms.

Sorting algorithms I am not yet familiar with:

Merge Sort – I don’t fully understand how the divide-and-conquer approach works.
Quick Sort – The partitioning process is still confusing to me.
Heap Sort – I am not familiar with how heaps are built and used for sorting.

Why I have not mastered them yet:

I have not practiced enough problems using these concepts.
Some concepts are still new to me.
I need more time and exercises to fully understand and apply them.
